<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<handout>
    <title>Average Rate of Change Practice! Section 1.3</title>

    <p>
        <alert>MTH 124</alert>
    </p>

    <activity>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                Suppose the total cost in dollars to produce x items is given by
                the function <m>C(x)</m>, and that
                <m>AV_{[100,200]} = 24.04</m>.
            </p>
        </introduction>

        <task workspace="0.3in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    What are the units of the average rate of change?
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution component="aaa-soln">
              <p>
                Output is cost in $, input is item, so units are $/item.
              </p>
            </solution>
        </task>

        <task workspace="0.5in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    What does <m>AV_{[100,200]} = 24.04</m> mean in context?
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution component="aaa-soln">
              <p>
                On average when producing between 100 and 200 items it
                costs $24.04 per item produced.
              </p>
            </solution>
        </task>

        <task workspace="0.5in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    If <m>AV_{[100,200]} = 24.04</m> and
                    <m>AV_{[200,300]}=36.04</m>, what can you say about
                    <m>C(x)</m>.
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution component="aaa-soln">
              <p>
                On average it costs more to produce an additional item if we have 
                between 200 and 300 items already, than it does 
                to produce an additional item if we have between 100 and 200 items already.
              </p>
            </solution>
        </task>
    </activity>

    <activity>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                Suppose an object is thrown upward with initial velocity of 32
                feet per second from a height of 50 feet.
                The height of the object t seconds after it is thrown is given
                by a function <m>h(t)</m>.
            </p>
        </introduction>

        <task workspace="1in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    If <m>AV_{[0,2]} = 0</m>, what are the units, and what does
                    that mean in context?
                </p>
            </statement>
             <solution component="aaa-soln">
              <p>
                Output is height in feet, input is time in seconds, so the units are: ft/s. 
                On average during the first 2 seconds the height was decreasing 0 ft/s, i.e. 
                the velocity was 0ft/s on average. (The key here is on average! It did go up and down...)
              </p> 
            </solution>
        </task>

        <task workspace="1in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    If <m>AV_{[2,4]} = -64</m>, what are the units, and what
                    does that mean in context?
                </p>
            </statement>
           <solution component="aaa-soln">
            <p>
              On average between 2 and 4 seconds the height 
              was decreasing 64 ft/s, or the velocity was -64ft/s on average
              between 2 and 4 seconds.
            </p>
           </solution>
        </task>
    </activity>

    <activity>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                There is a specific breed of bacteria whose global population
                after <m>t</m> months is given by the function
                <m>p(t) = 4t^5 + 4t^2+4240.</m>
            </p>
        </introduction>

        <task workspace="1in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    If the average rate of change of <m>p(t)</m> on the interval
                    from 0 to 6 is 5208, what does 5208 mean in context (include
                    units!)?
                </p>
            </statement>
             <solution component="aaa-soln">
              <p>
                On average during the first 6 months the population of 
                bacteria is increasing by 5208 bacteria per month.
              </p> 
            </solution>
        </task>

        <task workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    What is <m>AV_{[6,12]}</m>?
                    Include units.
                </p>
            </statement>
             <solution component="aaa-soln">
              <p>
                <m>AV_{[6,12]}=\frac{p(12)-p(6)}{12-6}=160,776</m> bacteria per month
              </p> 
            </solution>
        </task>
    </activity>

    <activity>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                The velocity of a skydiver is given by a function <m>v(t)</m>,
                where <m>v(t)</m> is in feet per second and <m>t</m> is in
                seconds.
            </p>
        </introduction>

        <task workspace="1in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    What would be the units or the average rate of change of
                    <m>v(t)</m>?
                </p>
            </statement>
             <solution component="aaa-soln">
              <p>
                Since output is velocity in ft/s and input is time in s, then the units are output over input, 
                or <m>\frac{ft/s}{s}</m>.  This is the same as <m>ft/s^2</m>, it's an acceleration!
              </p> 
            </solution>
        </task>

        <task workspace="1in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    If <m>AV_{[0,10]}=147</m>, what would that mean in context?
                    Use the units to help you!
                </p>
            </statement>
             <solution component="aaa-soln">
              <p>
                On average in the first 10 seconds the acceleration is <m>147 ft/s^2</m>, or 
                on average in the first 10 seconds the velocity is increasing by 147 ft/s per second.
              </p> 
            </solution>
        </task>

        <task workspace="1in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    The table below gives the velocity <m>v(t)</m> in 10 second
                    intervals.
                    Velocity is measured in feet per second (fps).
                </p>

                <tabular>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><term>Time in seconds</term></cell>
                        <cell>0</cell>
                        <cell>10</cell>
                        <cell>20</cell>
                        <cell>30</cell>
                        <cell>40</cell>
                        <cell>50</cell>
                        <cell>60</cell>
                    </row>

                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><term>Velocity in fps</term></cell>
                        <cell>0</cell>
                        <cell>147</cell>
                        <cell>171</cell>
                        <cell>175</cell>
                        <cell>175.8</cell>
                        <cell>176</cell>
                        <cell>176</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>

                <p>
                    Find <m>AV_{[50,60]}</m>.
                    What does it mean about the skydiver?
                </p>
            </statement>
             <solution component="aaa-soln">
              <p>
                <m>AV_{[50,60]}=\frac{v(60)-v(50)}{60-50}=\frac{176-176}{10}=0 ft/s^2</m>. 
                During that 10 second interval between 50 and 60 seconds, the skydiver has stopped accelerating (i.e.
                their velocity is not changing on average).  Free fall!
              </p> 
            </solution>
        </task>
    </activity>
</handout>